---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import DownloadPanel from "../components/DownloadPanel.svelte";
---
<SiteLayout title="Download saGraph">
  <Header />
  <main class="container page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h1>Put your workflows somewhere close.</h1>
    <p class="intro">Choose the package for your platform. saGraph runs as a local desktop panel; your task data is stored on the machine where you use it.</p>
    <DownloadPanel client:load />
    <div class="download-note card">
      <strong>Choose the package that fits your setup.</strong>
      <span>Installers are recommended for most people. Portable builds do not require installation. The updater archive is used by the desktop app and is not normally needed for a manual install.</span>
    </div>
    <section class="install-guide"><p class="eyebrow">Which file should I choose?</p><div class="guide-grid"><article><strong>Most people</strong><p>Use the installer for your platform. It creates the normal application entry and is the easiest way to receive updates.</p></article><article><strong>Portable setup</strong><p>Use the portable Windows build when you want to keep the app and its data together, such as on a work folder or removable drive.</p></article><article><strong>Linux packages</strong><p>Use AppImage for a self-contained download, or DEB for Debian and Ubuntu systems. Make the AppImage executable before launching it.</p></article></div></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .page { padding: 7rem 0 2rem; }
  .page h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); letter-spacing: -0.08em; line-height: 0.96; margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem; max-width: 800px; }
  .intro { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 650px; }
  .download-note { color: var(--muted); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem; }.install-guide { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 5rem; padding-top: 2rem; }.guide-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 1.4rem; }.guide-grid article { border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }.guide-grid strong { font-size: 0.92rem; }.guide-grid p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
  .download-note strong { color: var(--text); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .guide-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
